      "description": "Leatherstocking Gas Company, LLC is a regulated Pennsylvania natural gas utility serving Susquehanna and Bradford counties. Corning Natural Gas Holding Corporation and Mirabito Regulated Industries established related 50/50 Leatherstocking ventures in New York in 2010 and Pennsylvania in 2011. Corning acquired Mirabito's 50% Pennsylvania interest on July 1, 2020, becoming sole owner of the Pennsylvania utility; the separate New York Leatherstocking business became wholly owned by Mirabito and is outside this record's boundary. Argo Infrastructure Partners acquired the Corning parent through ACP Crotona Corp. on July 6, 2022, and the parent was renamed Corning Energy Corporation. Leatherstocking remains an active operating subsidiary beneath Corning rather than a separate manager-level Argo investment. It is therefore archived from the standalone PortCo census without a legal merge or redirect. The announced Apollo-Argo manager transaction was terminated in January 2026, and no later Leatherstocking sale, dissolution, rebrand or signed pending ownership transfer was identified through August 16, 2026.",
